OL,3,AShould promotion depend on how workers
OL,4,Ause AI?
OL,5,
OL,6,FIt's in Duncan Trevithick's interest to
OL,7,Fbe good at using AI at work - if he can
OL,8,Fuse it to get more tasks done, faster,
OL,9,Fhe'll qualify for a bonus at the end of
OL,10,Fthe year.
OL,12,FOn the surface, it's a great incentive.
OL,13,FBut he's questioning what's really in
OL,14,Fit for him.
OL,16,F"The uncomfortable interpretation is
OL,17,Fthat employees are being assessed on
OL,18,Fhow effectively they can participate in
OL,19,Ftheir own redundancy," says Spain-based
OL,20,FTrevithick, 34, who works in marketing
OL,21,Ffor an AI training data company.
OL,23,APub: 08-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG7/19
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
FL,109,105,200,160,0,100
